king for deterministic, isolated test runs.\n./docs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:246:- **Docker tag sync.** Dependabot updates to `allowed-docker-images` trigger `sync-docker-tags.yml`, which back-commits the synchronized tags into the Dependabot PR.\n./docs/architecture/tck.md:191:| `checkAllowedDockerImages` | Scan allowed images for vulnerabilities with grype, either all images or only those changed between two commits (§AR-scan-docker-images). |\n./docs/DEVELOPING.md:274:   ./gradlew checkAllowedDockerImages --baseCommit=$(git rev-parse origin/master) --newCommit=$(git rev-parse HEAD)\n./docs/DEVELOPING.md:279:   ./gradlew checkAllowedDockerImages\n./docs/DEVELOPING.md:333:- Scan changed Docker images: `./gradlew checkAllowedDockerImages --baseCommit=<sha1> --newCommit=<sha2>`\n./docs/DEVELOPING.md:334:- Scan all Docker images: `./gradlew checkAllowedDockerImages`\n./tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/resources/allowed-docker-images/Dockerfile-hashicorp_vault:1:FROM hashicorp/vault:1.20.4\n./tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/groovy/org.graalvm.internal.tck-harness.gradle:887:tasks.register(\"checkAllowedDockerImages\", GrypeTask.class) { task ->\n./tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/GrypeTask.java:31: * Implements §AR-test-harness.6 — the {@code checkAllowedDockerImages} task that scans allowed\n./tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/GrypeTask.java:54:    private static final String DOCKERFILE_DIRECTORY = \"allowed-docker-images\";\n./tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/GrypeTask.java:209:                    \"This task should be executed only if there are changes in allowed-docker-images directory.\");\n./tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/GrypeTask.java:221:            throw new RuntimeException(\"Cannot find allowed-docker-images directory\");\n./tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/java/org/graalvm/internal/tck/DockerUtils.java:20:    public static final String ALLO